# Close-out D4 (open decision 11): a succeeded, failed or cancelled job never changes status again. The fault removes the trigger (its CREATE TRIGGER and its COMMENT ON TRIGGER) from platform_0007; since platform_0011 a second wall stands behind it (the lifecycle guard jobs_transition_guard: a terminal status has no legal move), so a succeeded job is still REFUSED the move back to draft, but by job_transition_illegal and not by jobs_terminal_is_final, and the test must say so (refused, but not for the expected reason).
GATE=terminal-final
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestCloseout_TerminalSucceededIsFinal (database integration test, real Postgres)
CMD=H_PG_ADMIN_DSN="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" bash tests/harness/run-db-tests.sh '^TestCloseout_TerminalSucceededIsFinal$'
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestCloseout_TerminalSucceededIsFinal
MESSAGE=a succeeded job moved to draft by a bare UPDATE: refused, but not for the expected reason
